  ## Human intervention needed
  
  The automated job failed during dynamic-access test generation for `org.springframework.cloud:spring-cloud-vault-config:5.0.2`.
  
  Preserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fkimeta%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-9705-library-new-request-org.springframework.cloud-spring-cloud-vault-config-5.0.2-a9438eac
  
  The likely failure is coverage convergence, not Gradle or Native Image execution. After 6 iterations, the final report remained at 1/2 dynamic-access calls (50%). The uncovered call is `Field#set` at `VaultConfigDataLoader.java:424`. The generation log concludes that this path may be unreachable through the resolved public API because Spring Vault `4.0.3` exposes only a `protected final Log logger`, which `isUpdateableLogField` rejects; both final attempts therefore made no test changes. The class was recorded as exhausted.
  
  The generated Vault integration test itself passes: the latest Gradle log reports one successful native test and `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`. Metrics nevertheless record `status: failure`, `generated_loc: 0`, and `metadata_entries: 0`, indicating that finalization did not complete and the preserved branch is not publication-ready.
  
